Regression guard for the var collision of byte-identical interpolated declarations.

One module, two bindings (`header` and `bar`) carry the identical interpolated
declaration `background-color: $(Color.Background.Alt.box)`. A class name holds
no label, so the two bindings share one atom and one variable, and differ only
in their binding id.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input.re > output.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl output.ml -o output.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate output.ml > styles.css

The same declaration body resolves to a single variable across both bindings:

  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @property --box-26a144{syntax:"*";inherits:false;}
  ._a4lVB3cAy{background-color:var(--box-26a144);}
